Package: auto-yes
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Anticitoyen <anticitoyen@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: expect (>= 5.45)
Recommends: gnome-terminal
Homepage: https://github.com/AntiCitoyen/Anticitoyen-auto-yes
Description: Automatically answers "1" (Yes) to "Do you want to proceed?" prompts
 Two ways to use it:
 .
  - auto-yes <command> [args...] : wrap a single command, fully interactive
    (Ctrl-C, window resize, your own typing all pass through; the matched
    prompt is answered automatically).
  - auto-yes-shell : a drop-in replacement for your login shell that does the
    same for EVERY command typed in that terminal, with no prefix needed.
 .
 The matched prompt(s) live in /etc/auto-yes/patterns.conf, one Tcl regexp per
 line, re-read on every new terminal (no rebuild needed to add a pattern).
 .
 Warning: this silently confirms ANY prompt matching a configured pattern in a
 wrapped terminal, including from destructive commands (package removal, disk
 tools) or from another program's own approval prompts. Keep the pattern list
 narrow.
